        "original_id": "fcdb8b86-6346-547e-9830-5ddfad1cf0c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Lansing State Journal, Gannett\n- Places: Lansing, Michigan, Ingham County, Eaton County, Clinton County, Michigan\n- Topics: newspaper ownership, state capitals, population\n\nFacts:\n- Lansing is the capital of the U.S. state of Michigan.\n- Lansing is mostly in Ingham County, with portions extending into Eaton County and Clinton County.\n- In the 2010 Census, Lansing had a population of 114,297 and was the fifth largest city in Michigan.\n- The Lansing State Journal is a daily newspaper published in Lansing, Michigan.\n- Gannett owns the Lansing State Journal.",
